			<div class="content" id="post-content-4773571">
									

<p><strong>There is meaning in your lives. You are loved, you are wanted, you are appreciated. And you are unique. The variety of experiences which constitute our race is beautiful. You are valid, you are meaningful, and you deserve life. Live it on your own terms, and accept no definitions, no impositions, but your own. Only you know who you are. Revel in the knowledge.</strong></p>
<p>And that's the end of my Site-43 history trilogy. It's not the end of history, though. So that's nice.</p>
<p>It's also probably the last thing you'll hear about Site-43 until the end of the Canon Renaissance Contest. I'm sure you'll survive. Not hearing about Site-43, that is; whether or not you survive the Canon Renaissance Contest depends on a lot more variables.</p>
<p>I could have twisted the knife harder, but some of this material is very personal to me, so I didn't. When I eventually write the companion tale, I'll be sure to absolutely devastate myself for you.</p>
<p>Many thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4558017&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605358959" alt="Grigori Karpin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4558017)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;">Grigori Karpin</a></span> for his crit, and an excellent suggestion about the ending (that there should in fact be one).</p>
