														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4773635">
									

<p>There’s a lot here.</p>
<p>There are a few authors who I’ll see have posted on LC and immediately go and read the articles, I’m happy to add your name to that ever growing list.</p>
<p>As for the actual article, this is phenomenal story telling. This almost felt like a Series 1 or early Series 2 SCP in the best of ways, and I really don’t know why. Maybe it’s the dialogue or the structure, maybe the simplistic anomaly?Regardless, I enjoyed this front and back, especially those notes. Something I have trouble with and I think other authors have trouble with is attempting to write a believable cognitive breakdown, and this does a really good job of subtlety conveying that there’s something wrong here. Dr. Scout was a real highlight here too, good motivations and watching the hatred and grief build up was great.</p>
<p>Those exploration logs were solid, although they were not the highlight for me and fell slightly flat, but I see their use in the narrative and they didn’t go on long enough for me to knock anything.</p>
<p>I’d be amiss to not talk about the ending. At first I didn’t see a reason for the email following that final note, but what a punch in the gut was that final paragraph?</p>
<p>Again, another great job. I’m looking forward to your next post. +1</p>

							</div>

								
