					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harryblank" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6479803); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6479803&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238090" alt="HarryBlank" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6479803)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harryblank" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6479803); return false;" >HarryBlank</a></span> <span class="odate time_1605356594 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Nov 2020 12:23</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4818279">
									

<p>Wow, that was unexpected to say the least. Thank you so much for sharing all of that with me, and allowing yourself to be seen in this way. It was very brave, and it means a lot to me that you felt that connection.</p>
<p>Six thousand SCP files, and you find one that so closely parallels your feelings&#8230; how unlikely! Working through a problem like that and making a difference in the world is truly noble. Even if you've only described your contributions to science and society in abstract terms, know that they are worthwhile, as are you.</p>
<p>Your life has value, and as long as there's a spark in your soul there's a reason to live; the part with Scout's attempt was meant to be a commentary on assisted suicide and dignity for the elderly, not on suicide or euthanasia for the neurodivergent. I'm mentally ill myself, though not in the same way, so I would never have meant it like that.</p>
<p>But I'm very interested to hear that you saw yourself reflected in the bulk of this piece; I expected that to happen as little as you did! It must have come as a shock. I hope I handled the topic tastefully, and didn't make life more difficult for you. Thank you for reaching out, and you're more than welcome to write, draw, or do whatever comes to mind in relation to this SCP. I'd be pleased to see what you come up with, or even help, but no pressure. I recognize the difficulties you face, though I can only imagine what the experience is actually like.</p>
<p>Stay safe, and best of luck. We're all in the dark some times, but there's clarity in communication, so I'm glad we could have this conversation. Whether you remember it or not, I will, and you made a definite and lasting difference in my experience of this piece.</p>

							</div>

								
